      "writtenOn": "2026-11-10T09:19:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for checking. encodeRequestCommonHeader() packs 6 bytes (5-byte header + command), while commonRequestSize is 7 because it already includes the data size byte. So the port number is the only extra byte: 5 + 1 + 1 + 1 \u003d 8 \u003d commonRequestSize + 1. The Ethernet variant uses + 2 for its 16-bit port the same way. EncodeGetPortTelemetryCountersRequestSuccess encodes into a buffer of exactly this size and returns 0.",
      "parentUuid": "780c7fa8_b617401f",
